WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.780
Connie's house wasn't the only thing&nbsp;
that got demolished in the Young Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.460
finale — our hearts did, too. And one&nbsp;
scene in particular had fans sobbing.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.840
Longtime fans of the "Big Bang Theory" spin-off&nbsp;
"Young Sheldon" know all too well that the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.700
has no trouble reining in the comedy in exchange&nbsp;
for heartfelt and dramatic moments. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.840
even they weren't prepared for what the&nbsp;
Season 6 finale, "A Tornado, a 10-Hour Flight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.800
and a Darn Fine Ring," brought them.&nbsp;
When a tornado touches down in Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.520
the shock of the disaster prompts the&nbsp;
scattered members of the Cooper clan to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.640
reconsider their interpersonal&nbsp;
relationships and situations.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.000
There are plenty of emotional moments&nbsp;
from the episode to go around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.380
but viewers were especially struck by the&nbsp;
scene where Cooper family patriarch George&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:45.300
Sr. and Missy reconcile over their recently&nbsp;
frayed relationship while stuck on the side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.900
of the road. Missy, who has been dealing&nbsp;
with quite a bit of teenage angst lately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.920
owns up to her recent actions, while&nbsp;
George does his best to comfort her.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:58.740
After the episode aired on May 18, 2023, many&nbsp;
fans online were vocal regarding how this scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.220
as well as the rest of the episode,&nbsp;
made them feel. As one Redditor wrote:

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.880
"I started crying when George and Missy were&nbsp;
hugging each other on the side of the road."

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.420
As it turns out, they were far from&nbsp;
the only person who shed some tears.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.380
Several "Young Sheldon" fans noted that&nbsp;
they were surprised by how much they reacted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.940
emotionally to George and Missy's bonding&nbsp;
scenes and the Season 6 finale in general.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.440
"I don't think I've ever cried at a show like&nbsp;
I did with this one. Missy and George bonding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.860
moment was killer and then following it&nbsp;
up with Connie's house being destroyed."

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.340
Even fans who weren't as hot on the&nbsp;
overall episode and its plotlines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.160
found the moment quite compelling. One user noted:

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.300
"I really didn't like the use of a tornado to&nbsp;
resolve everyone's feelings after a fight for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:41.100
second time, but they did it just as well as the&nbsp;
first time. I cried at the end at Connie's house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.600
and George's ability to step in and protect&nbsp;
himself and Missy. Incredibly endearing."

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.020
"I'm sorry. I'm sorry for everything."

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.920
Particular praise was heaped upon&nbsp;
Raegan Revord's performance as Missy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.740
as fans found her to be the&nbsp;
standout character of the episode.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:00.960
Even while fans on Reddit discussed how much they&nbsp;
loved George Sr. and Missy's emotional moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.280
several other parts of the episode came&nbsp;
up in conversation. The destruction of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.300
Meemaw's house and the overall chemistry of the&nbsp;
"Young Sheldon" cast members were discussed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.500
as were the unexpected actions of the&nbsp;
often shady and condescending Pastor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.460
Jeff Difford. Instead of ratting her out,&nbsp;
he keeps his lips sealed about the gambling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.060
room Meemaw runs within her laundromat&nbsp;
— largely because of the fate of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.900
home and the traumatic experience they&nbsp;
just endured in the form of the tornado.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:30.240
One Reddit user described Jeff's uncharacteristic&nbsp;
decision as one of the highlights of the Season 6&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.080
finale, while another fan feels this&nbsp;
was a rare example of Jeff choosing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.820
his humanity over his faith. Still, one&nbsp;
person isn't exactly overjoyed by Jeff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.720
choosing to look out for Meemaw, calling&nbsp;
him out for his inconsistency, writing:

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.380
"Why can't he forgive the "sin" of&nbsp;
Georgie getting Mandy pregnant out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.920
of wedlock when this guys first wife&nbsp;
hated him so much and then left him."

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.660
All in all, the closer of "Young Sheldon"&nbsp;
Season 6, "A Tornado, a 10-Hour Flight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.800
and a Darn Fine Ring," doesn't seem to&nbsp;
have left fans of the show disappointed.

